<title>SOUTH AFRICA: JCI in talks on possible sale of coal unit.</title>
<headline>JCI in talks on possible sale of coal unit.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African mining house JCI Ltd said on Monday it was in early stage discussion on the possible sale of its coal business.</p>
<p>It said it would issue a cautionary announcement in Tuesday's press, but gave no further details.  </p>
<p>JCI's wholly-owned subsidiary, Tavistock Colliery Ltd, recently acquired Shell South Africa's coal business for 440 million rand, which it said at the time would complement Tavistock's export drive.</p>
